{
  "id" : "lofty_irisil_pyramidtrap5",
  "title" : "Effective Trap Design 5/5",
  "description" : "Final thoughts on traps: strengths vs. limitations.",
  "icon" : "lofty_irisil_pyramidtrap5.png",
  
  "contentPages" : [
"^yellow;Chapter 5: Final Thoughts^reset;

With all of the information that's been covered so far in mind, it's important to step back and put the craft of trapping a lair in perspective.

Ideally, your traps will catch a victim off guard, and usually that's enough. Sometimes, however, traps don't finish the job.

^cyan;Always have a backup plan.^reset;

^#8888CC;>>",

"^yellow;Chapter 5: Final Thoughts^reset;

^green;If you're out of options, ask for help.^reset;

Veteran adventurers survive traps, but for as nimble as they might be, ^red;they're not usually terribly clever.^reset; Simply asking them to go fight monsters on your behalf is often enough incentive for adventurers!

^#888888;Being cute helps a lot here, but keep some pixels ready in case you need to use a bribe instead.^reset;
^#8888CC;>>",

"^yellow;Chapter 5: Final Thoughts^reset;

^green;Sometimes you just have to kill them yourself.^reset;

If interlopers have made it all the way to your personal chambers, thwarted your traps, and dispatched of your minions, you may occasionally have to get your hands dirty.

Most adventurers are gullible, though, ^cyan;so just stab them in the back if you can get away with it.^reset;
^#8888CC;>>",

"^yellow;Chapter 5: Final Thoughts^reset;

^green;Let the door hit them on the way out.^reset;

While it's technically riskier, another approach to dealing with especially troublesome adventurers is to simply let them load up on treasure before trying to actually kill them.

Placing traps along the exit route to target intruders who have their hands full works great for small parties, but lacks staying power against raids.
^#8888CC;>>",

"^yellow;Chapter 5: Final Thoughts^reset;

^green;There's always another lair.^reset;

If all else fails, ^cyan;it's better to relocate to a new dungeon than it is to be slain at the end of one.^reset;

You can always occupy another crypt, erect another wizard tower, corrupt another temple from within, etc- and the change of scenery can be nice, too. Variety in life is good!

^#8888CC;>>",

"^yellow;Chapter 5: Final Thoughts^reset;

^green;In a universe full of treasure to collect, there's always room for a few more deadly surprises.^reset;

Hopefully this guide helps your lair become a haven for you and a beacon for prosperity!

^red;...Delivered to you one dead adventurer at a time."

  ],
    "itemConfig" : {
    "rarity" : "Common",
    "price" : 25
  }
}
